This repository includes a shared native-panel integration for ReadWeave. It reuses
the upstream ReadWeave Panel and distributes its built panel, chunks, styles and
assets with LessonWeave. ReadWeave is maintained separately upstream.

`integrations/readweave/native-licenses/INDEX.md` maps the packages used by the
native bundle to their original license and notice files. That directory also
contains ReadWeave's AGPL license and the dependency notices. The package list is
derived from `integrations/readweave/native-build.json`.

The public ReadWeave source snapshot used to build the shared panel is available
with the [LessonWeave v0.2.0 Release](https://github.com/AIALRA-0/AIALRA-LessonWeave/releases/tag/v0.2.0).

Runtime dependencies retain their respective licenses, including PyMuPDF,
Playwright, Beautiful Soup, Requests, jsonschema, markdown-it-py, Pillow,
and tree-sitter-language-pack. Docling is an optional parser integration.
The Codex CLI is installed separately from the official OpenAI distribution.

The architecture viewer bundles Mermaid 10.9.3 under the MIT license.
Its license is preserved in framework/architecture/vendor/LICENSE-mermaid.txt.
The reader also bundles Mermaid and KaTeX 0.16.22 under their retained MIT licenses
in framework/reader/media-vendor.

The repository's examples are self-authored synthetic materials.
User-supplied materials and generated private books are not distributed here.

ReplayWeb.page 2.5.3 is redistributed without modification under AGPL-3.0-or-later.
Its license is preserved in framework/reader/archive/LICENSE-ReplayWeb.page.txt.
Source: https://github.com/webrecorder/replayweb.page/tree/v2.5.3
Browsertrix Crawler 1.15.0 runs as a separately installed container.
warcio 1.7.5 retains its Apache-2.0 license.
